@lang en
-- tests-independent.l4: an independent test author's assertions for the Interpretation Act (British Columbia) encoding.
-- Expected values come from ../ANSWERS.md. Scenarios 1-549 were written from the source text BEFORE any .l4 file was opened.
-- Scenarios 550-576 (the addendum section) were added after I had read the module source; their expected values are still from the text.
-- Scenario numbers are those of ANSWERS.md. Nothing was edited to match the encoding's output without a record. Where triage afterwards changed an expected value, the `-- RECONCILED` comment above the assertion quotes the original and gives the reason.
--
-- How a scenario is turned into an assertion:
--   * a yes/no answer of Y is asserted as the encoding's TRUE for the matching question; N as NOT (...), i.e. FALSE;
--   * where my answer is "not covered" (NC) the assertion is `#ASSERT REFUSED`, the encoding's own convention;
--   * a scenario for which the encoding exports no function is listed as a GAP in the comment block at the end.
-- Holiday and office calendars are inputs to the encoding; the ones below are mine (Sunday and 26 December are
-- supplied by the encoding's `s 29 a day is a holiday`; the other fixed-date holidays are added by me).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-periods`
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-commencement`
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-definitions`
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-repeal`
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-replacement`
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-reading`
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-powers`
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-terms`

§ `Test helpers (mine)`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test: my other holidays` d MEANS
        (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 25)
    OR  (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 1)
    OR  (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 7 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 1)
    OR  (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 9 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 30)
    OR  (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 11 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 11)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test: my holiday calendar` d MEANS `s 29 a day is a holiday` `test: my other holidays` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test: office open Monday to Friday` d MEANS (`Weekday of` d AT LEAST 1) AND (`Weekday of` d AT MOST 5)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test: office regularly closed at weekends` d MEANS NOT (`test: office open Monday to Friday` d)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test: office open Monday to Friday except Monday 13 January 2025` d MEANS (`test: office open Monday to Friday` d) AND NOT (d EQUALS YMD 2025 1 13)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test: office never regularly closed` d MEANS FALSE

GIVEN u IS A `Unit of a period`
      n IS A NUMBER
      c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Period of time`
`test: period` u n c MEANS `Period of time` WITH `unit` IS u, `how many` IS n, `clear` IS c

GIVEN m IS A `Pacific Time moment`
      d IS A DATE
      h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test: moment is` m d h MEANS
    (m's `calendar day` EQUALS d) AND (m's `hour of the day` EQUALS h) AND (m's `minute of the hour` EQUALS 0)

GIVEN mm IS A MAYBE `Pacific Time moment`
      d  IS A DATE
      h  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test: maybe moment is` mm d h MEANS
    CONSIDER mm
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST m THEN `test: moment is` m d h

GIVEN m IS A `UTC moment`
      d IS A DATE
      h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`test: UTC moment is` m d h MEANS
    (m's `calendar day` EQUALS d) AND (m's `hour of the day` EQUALS h) AND (m's `minute of the hour` EQUALS 0)

§ `s 1 Definitions (scenarios 1-21)`

-- 1 [s 1 Act, l.10] statute called a code, enacted by the Legislature: Y
#ASSERT `s 1 an instrument is an Act` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) TRUE FALSE
-- 2 [s 1 Act, l.10] 1865 ordinance with force of law, referring to past legislation: Y
#ASSERT `s 1 an instrument is an Act` FALSE TRUE (YMD 1865 6 1) TRUE TRUE
-- 3 [s 1 Act, l.10] 1860 proclamation with force of law, referring to past legislation: Y
#ASSERT `s 1 an instrument is an Act` FALSE TRUE (YMD 1860 1 1) TRUE TRUE
-- 4 [s 1 Act, l.10] 1871 ordinance with force of law, referring to past legislation: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 an instrument is an Act` FALSE TRUE (YMD 1871 6 1) TRUE TRUE)
-- 5 [s 1 Act, l.10; s 29 Legislature l.266] statute of the Parliament of Canada: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 an instrument is an Act` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) TRUE FALSE)
-- 6 [s 1 Act, l.10] 1865 ordinance NOT referring to past legislation: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 an instrument is an Act` FALSE TRUE (YMD 1865 1 1) TRUE FALSE)
-- 7 [s 1 enact, l.11] includes prescribe: Y
#ASSERT `s 29 the definition of a term names a thing` "enact" `In an enactment` "prescribe"
-- 8 [s 1 enact, l.11] includes issue: Y
#ASSERT `s 29 the definition of a term names a thing` "enact" `In an enactment` "issue"
-- 9 [s 1 enactment, l.12] a portion of a regulation is an enactment: Y
#ASSERT `s 1 a thing is an enactment` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- 10 [s 1 enactment, l.12] a court judgment is an enactment: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 a thing is an enactment` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- 11 [s 1 public officer, l.13] person in the public service of BC: Y
#ASSERT `s 29 the definition of a term names a thing` "public officer" `In an enactment` "a person in the public service of British Columbia"
-- 12 [s 1 regulation, l.14-16 restored] bylaw enacted in execution of a power under an Act: Y
#ASSERT `s 1 an instrument is a regulation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 13 [s 1 regulation, l.14-16 restored] order enacted by or under the authority of the LGIC: Y
#ASSERT `s 1 an instrument is a regulation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- 14 [s 1 regulation, l.14] tariff of fees under a power conferred by an Act: Y
#ASSERT `s 1 an instrument is a regulation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 15 [s 1 regulation, l.14] order of a court made in the course of an action: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 an instrument is a regulation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- 16 [s 1 regulation, l.14] order of an administrative tribunal in a dispute between 2 persons: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 an instrument is a regulation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- 17 [s 1 regulation, l.14] order of a public officer in a dispute between 2 persons: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 an instrument is a regulation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- 18 [s 1 regulation, l.14-16 restored] private club rule, neither under an Act nor by the LGIC: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 an instrument is a regulation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- 19 [s 1 repeal, l.17] includes rescind: Y
#ASSERT `s 29 the definition of a term names a thing` "repeal" `In an enactment` "rescind"
-- 20 [s 1 repeal, l.17] includes revoke: Y
#ASSERT `s 29 the definition of a term names a thing` "repeal" `In an enactment` "revoke"
-- 21 [s 1 repeal, l.17] includes cancel: Y
#ASSERT `s 29 the definition of a term names a thing` "repeal" `In an enactment` "cancel"

§ `s 2 Application (22-27)`

-- 22 [s 2(1), l.20] a provision applies to an enactment enacted before commencement (no contrary intention): Y
#ASSERT `s 2(1) a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` FALSE FALSE
-- 23 [s 2(1), l.20] contrary intention in the enactment: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(1) a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` FALSE TRUE)
-- 24 [s 2(1), l.20] contrary intention in this Act: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(1) a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` TRUE FALSE)
-- 25 [s 2(2), l.21] the provisions of this Act apply to this Act: Y
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the provisions of this Act apply to the enactment` `This Act`
-- 26 [s 2(3), l.22] applicable rule of construction not inconsistent with this Act is preserved: Y
#ASSERT `s 2(3) a rule of construction is preserved by this Act` TRUE FALSE
-- 27 [s 2(3), l.22] rule of construction inconsistent with this Act is preserved: N
-- RECONCILED 27: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(3) a rule of construction is preserved by this Act` TRUE TRUE)`; triaged against the text: s 2(3) (l.22) speaks only of a rule of construction applicable to the enactment and not inconsistent with the Act; it says nothing about an inconsistent one (reviewer's verdict: its scenario wrong)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2(3) a rule of construction is preserved by this Act` TRUE TRUE

§ `s 3 Date of commencement (28-40)`

-- 28 [s 3(2), l.26] no commencement provision, assent 2025-05-10: 2025-05-10
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the date of commencement of a portion of an Act` (JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)) `It provides no date of commencement` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)
-- 29 [s 3(3), l.27] comes into force on proclamation, assent 2025-05-10: commencement provision in force on 2025-05-10
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the day the commencement provision and the title of an Act are in force` (JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)
-- 30 [s 3(3), l.27] same Act, proclamation already issued for 2026-01-01: the title is in force on 2025-05-10
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the day the commencement provision and the title of an Act are in force` (JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1))) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)
-- 31 [s 3(3), l.27] same Act, no proclamation yet: the operative provisions are in force on the date of assent: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(2) the date of commencement of a portion of an Act` (JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 5 10))
-- 32 [s 3(3), l.27] comes into force on 2025-09-01, assent 2025-05-10: title in force on 2025-05-10
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the day the commencement provision and the title of an Act are in force` (JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on a stated day` (YMD 2025 9 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)
-- 33 [s 3(3.1)(a), l.29] provision says 2025-01-01, assent 2025-05-10: comes into force on 2025-01-01
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the date of commencement of a portion of an Act` (JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on a stated day` (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- 34 [s 3(3.1)(b), l.30] same: retroactive to the earlier date: Y
#ASSERT `s 3(3.1) a portion comes into force on a day earlier than the date of assent, and is retroactive` (JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on a stated day` (YMD 2025 1 1))
-- 35 [s 3(3.1), l.28] provision says 2025-09-01 (later than assent): s 3(3.1) retroactivity applies: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(3.1) a portion comes into force on a day earlier than the date of assent, and is retroactive` (JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on a stated day` (YMD 2025 9 1)))
-- 36 [s 3(1), l.25] reserved Act, LG assented 2025-03-01, signification 2025-06-15: date of assent 2025-06-15
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the date of assent to an Act` (`The Act was reserved for the signification of the pleasure of the Governor General` (JUST (YMD 2025 6 15))) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 6 15)
-- 37 [s 3(4), l.31] the date of assent is part of the Act: Y
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the date is part of the Act` `The date of assent`
-- 38 [s 3(5), l.32] exempt regulation, no day expressed, enacted 2025-04-02: in force 2025-04-02
#ASSERT `s 3(5) the day a regulation comes into force` (YMD 2025 4 2) `A regulation of a class exempted from the Regulations Act, or to which that Act does not apply` `It is not expressed to come into force on a particular day` EQUALS YMD 2025 4 2
-- 39 [s 3(5), l.32] exempt regulation expressed to come into force 2025-05-01: s 3(5) fixes its commencement at the enactment day: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(5) the day a regulation comes into force` (YMD 2025 4 2) `A regulation of a class exempted from the Regulations Act, or to which that Act does not apply` (`It is expressed to come into force on a particular day` (YMD 2025 5 1)) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 2)
-- 40 [s 3(5), l.32] non-exempt regulation, no day expressed: NC
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 3(5) the day a regulation comes into force` (YMD 2025 4 2) `A regulation of any other class` `It is not expressed to come into force on a particular day`

§ `s 4 Time of commencement or repeal (41-49)`

-- 41 [s 4(1), l.35] in force on 2025-07-01: commences at the beginning of 2025-07-01 (00:00)
#ASSERT `test: moment is` (`s 4(1) the beginning of a day` (YMD 2025 7 1)) (YMD 2025 7 1) 0
-- 42 [s 3(2), s 4(1), l.26, 35] Act assented 2025-05-10, no other date: commences at the beginning of 2025-05-10
#ASSERT `test: maybe moment is` (`the moment from which a portion of an Act binds` (JUST (YMD 2025 5 10)) `It provides no date of commencement`) (YMD 2025 5 10) 0
-- 43 [s 4(2), l.36] replaced; new enactment commences 2025-07-01: old ceases at the beginning of 2025-07-01
#ASSERT `test: moment is` (`s 4(2) the moment an enactment that is repealed and replaced ceases to have effect` (YMD 2025 7 1)) (YMD 2025 7 1) 0
-- 44 [s 4(3), l.37] expires 2025-12-31: ceases at the end of 2025-12-31 (= 2026-01-01 00:00)
#ASSERT `test: moment is` (`s 4(3) the moment any other enactment ceases to have effect` (YMD 2025 12 31)) (YMD 2026 1 1) 0
-- 46 [s 4(3), l.37] otherwise ceases 2025-12-31: ceases at the end of 2025-12-31
#ASSERT `test: moment is` (`s 4(3) the end of a day` (YMD 2025 12 31)) (YMD 2026 1 1) 0
-- 48 [s 4(4), l.38] expired enactment deemed repealed for the purposes of this Act: Y
#ASSERT `s 4(4) the enactment is deemed to be repealed for the purposes of this Act` TRUE

§ `s 5 Preliminary proceedings and staggered commencement (50-57)`

-- 51 [s 5(1), l.41] regulation made before commencement has effect before commencement, not necessary to make it effective: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(1) a thing done before commencement has effect on a day` (YMD 2025 7 1) (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE)
-- 52 [s 5(1), l.41] same, insofar as necessary to make the enactment effective: Y
#ASSERT `s 5(1) a thing done before commencement has effect on a day` (YMD 2025 7 1) (YMD 2025 6 1) TRUE
-- 54 [s 5(2)(a), l.43] on proclamation: a proclamation may apply to one provision: Y
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of the provision` `On proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` TRUE
-- 55 [s 5(2)(b), l.44] proclamations may be issued at different times for different provisions: Y
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(b) the proclamations or regulations may be issued at different times` `On proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` TRUE
-- 56 [s 5(2), l.42] enactment to be repealed by regulation of the LGIC: s 5(2)(a) applies to the repeal of a provision: Y
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of the provision` `By regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` TRUE
-- 57 [s 5(2), l.42] enactment to come into force by ministerial order: s 5(2)(a) applies: N
-- RECONCILED 57: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(2)(a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of the provision` `In some other way` TRUE)`; triaged against the text: s 5(2) (l.42) speaks only of an enactment to come into force or be repealed on proclamation or by LGIC regulation; a ministerial order is outside it (reviewer's verdict: its scenario wrong)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 5(2)(a) the proclamation or regulation may apply to the coming into force or repeal of the provision` `In some other way` TRUE

§ `ss 6-10 (58-74)`

-- 58 [s 6, l.47] private Act provision, person not referred to or mentioned: does not affect the right
#ASSERT `s 6 what a provision in an Act does to a person's right` `A private Act` FALSE EQUALS `The provision does not affect the right`
-- 59 [s 6, l.47] private Act provision, person referred to or mentioned: affects the right (as the Act says)
#ASSERT `s 6 what a provision in an Act does to a person's right` `A private Act` TRUE EQUALS `The provision affects the right only as the Act refers to or mentions it`
-- 60 [s 7(2), l.51] present-tense provision applies to a circumstance as it arises: Y
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the provision applies to the circumstance as it arises` `Present tense` TRUE
-- 61 [s 7(1), l.50] enactment of 1990 read only as of its enactment day: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(1) the day as of which an enactment is read` (YMD 1990 1 1) (YMD 2030 1 1) EQUALS YMD 1990 1 1)
-- 64 [s 8.1(1), l.58] Declaration means as in the Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples Act: Y
