-- 66 [s 8.1(1), l.60] regulation in s 8.1 means as in the Regulations Act: Y
#ASSERT elem "Regulations Act" (`s 29 what the definition of a term points at` "regulation" `In section 8.1`)
-- 67 [s 8.1(1), l.60; s 1 l.14] regulation in s 8.1 takes its meaning from s 1: N
#ASSERT `s 29 how a term is defined` "regulation" `In section 8.1` EQUALS JUST `Has the same meaning as in another enactment or agreement`
-- 68 [s 8.1(2), l.61] a construction that abrogates or derogates from s 35 rights is open: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8.1(2) a construction of an enactment is open` TRUE)
-- 69 [s 8.1(3), l.62] a construction of an Act inconsistent with the Declaration is open: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8.1(3) a construction of the enactment is open` `An Act` FALSE)
-- 70 [s 9, l.65] the title is part of the enactment: Y
#ASSERT `s 9 the part is part of the enactment` `The title`
-- 71 [s 9, l.65] the preamble is intended to assist in explaining meaning and object: Y
#ASSERT `s 9 the part is intended to assist in explaining the meaning and object of the enactment` `The preamble`
-- 74 [s 10, l.68] the stated form of enacting clause is permitted: Y
#ASSERT `s 10 the enacting clause of an Act of the Legislature may be in this form` (`the form of enacting clause that s 10 gives`)

