§ `s 17 Corporate rights and powers (102-115)`

-- 102 [s 17(1), l.97] perpetual succession: Y
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation has perpetual succession`
-- 103 [s 17(1)(a), l.98] sue and be sued in its corporate name: Y
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` `Sue and be sued in its corporate name`
-- 104 [s 17(1)(b), l.99] contract and be contracted with: Y
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` `Contract and be contracted with in its corporate name`
-- 105 [s 17(1)(c), l.100] have a common seal and alter it: Y
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` `Have a common seal, and alter or change it`
-- 106 [s 17(1)(d), l.101] s 17(1)(d) confers power to acquire and dispose of land: N
-- RECONCILED 106: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT NOT (`s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` (`Acquire or dispose of property` TRUE TRUE))`; triaged against the text: genuine fork F-limit-or-scope (with F-open-list): the words mark the edge of what the provision speaks of, and the section does not say what follows outside it, so the encoding refuses; the reviewer wrote N (for land) and called the two conventions colliding, low stakes
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` (`Acquire or dispose of property` TRUE TRUE)
-- 107 [s 17(1)(d), l.101] s 17(1)(d) confers power to acquire and dispose of other property for its purposes: Y
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` (`Acquire or dispose of property` FALSE TRUE)
-- 108 [s 17(1)(e), l.102] regulate its own procedure and business: Y
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` `Regulate its own procedure and business`
-- 109 [s 17(1)(f), l.103] corporation with English and French name forms may use either or both: Y
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` (`Use either form of its name or both, and show both forms on its seal or have 2 seals` TRUE)
-- 110 [s 17(1)(f), l.103] such a corporation may have 2 seals: Y
#ASSERT `s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` (`Use either form of its name or both, and show both forms on its seal or have 2 seals` TRUE)
-- 111 [s 17(2), l.104] 3 of 5 members' acts bind the others and the corporation: Y
