§ `ss 27-28 (305-324)`

-- 305 [s 27(1), l.207] thing to be done before a judge whose jurisdiction extends to the place: Y
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the thing may be done by or before the official` `A judge` TRUE TRUE
-- 306 [s 27(1), l.207] ...before a judge whose jurisdiction does not extend to the place: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27(1) the thing may be done by or before the official` `A judge` TRUE FALSE)
-- 307 [s 27(2), l.208] power to do an act includes all powers necessary to enable it: Y
#ASSERT `s 27(2) the power is deemed to be given` TRUE TRUE
-- 308 [s 27(3), l.209] a power may be exercised from time to time as occasion requires
#ASSERT `s 27(3) when a power may be exercised or a duty must be performed` `A power` EQUALS `The power may be exercised from time to time as occasion requires`
-- 309 [s 27(3), l.209] a duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires
#ASSERT `s 27(3) when a power may be exercised or a duty must be performed` `A duty` EQUALS `The duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires`
-- 310 [s 27(4), l.210] a power to make regulations includes the power to repeal them: Y
#ASSERT `s 27(4) a power to make regulations includes the power` `Repeal the regulations` TRUE
-- 311 [s 27(4), l.210] ...exercisable subject to the same consent as the original making: Y
#ASSERT (`s 27(4) how the included power to repeal, amend or make others is exercised` (`How a power is exercised` WITH `the manner` IS "order in council", `the consent and conditions, if any` IS LIST "consent of the Minister"))'s `the consent and conditions, if any` EQUALS LIST "consent of the Minister"
-- 312 [s 27(5), l.211] authorized act dependent on an act of the LGIC: the LGIC has power to do that other act: Y
#ASSERT `s 27(5) the one who must do the other act has the power to do it` `The Lieutenant Governor in Council` TRUE
-- 313 [s 27(5), l.211] ...dependent on an act of a private person: s 27(5) gives that person power: N
