§ `ss 29.1-29.2 (448-466)`

-- 448 [s 29.1(1), l.333] the s 29.1 definitions apply in a treaty first nation enactment: "treaty first nation" is defined there
#ASSERT `s 29 how a term is defined` "treaty first nation" `In all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters` EQUALS JUST `Means`
-- 449 [s 29.1(1), l.333] ...in an enactment about highway traffic (scope: an enactment): "treaty first nation" is defined there: N
#ASSERT `s 29 the definition of a term` "treaty first nation" `In an enactment` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 450 [s 29.1(1), l.345] a citizen of a treaty first nation under its laws is a constituent
#ASSERT `s 29 the words the Act gives for a term` "treaty first nation constituent" `In all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters` EQUALS JUST "an individual who is a citizen of the treaty first nation under the laws of the treaty first nation"
-- 451 [s 29.1(1), l.346] an individual enrolled under the final agreement is a member
#ASSERT `s 29 the words the Act gives for a term` "treaty first nation member" `In all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters` EQUALS JUST "an individual who is enrolled under the final agreement of the treaty first nation"
-- 452 [s 29.1(1), l.343] a constituent who has not reached the age of majority is a treaty first nation child: Y
#ASSERT `s 29 the definition of a term names a thing` "treaty first nation child" `In all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters` "a treaty first nation constituent who has not reached the age of majority"
-- 453 [s 29.1(1), l.343-344] a member who HAS reached the age of majority is a treaty first nation child: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 29 the definition of a term names a thing` "treaty first nation child" `In all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters` "a treaty first nation member who has reached the age of majority")
-- 454 [s 29.1(1), l.340] a first nation that is a party to a final agreement is a treaty first nation: Y
#ASSERT `s 29 the definition of a term names a thing` "treaty first nation" `In all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters` "a first nation that is a party to a final agreement"
-- 455 [s 29.1(1), l.341] the government of such a first nation is a treaty first nation: Y
#ASSERT `s 29 the definition of a term names a thing` "treaty first nation" `In all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters` "the government, as constituted under the final agreement and constitution, of such a first nation"
-- 456 [s 29.1(1), l.337] an Act of the Province ratifying an agreement that will be a final agreement is settlement legislation
#ASSERT `s 29 the words the Act gives for a term` "settlement legislation" `In all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters` EQUALS JUST "an Act of the Province ratifying and giving the force of law to an agreement that, on coming into effect, will be a final agreement"
-- 458 [s 29.1(1), l.334] "final agreement" carries the exception for references to the Nisga'a Final Agreement
#ASSERT elem "except in references to the Nisg̱a'a Final Agreement" (`s 29 the conditions a definition of a term carries` "final agreement" `In all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters`)
-- 459 [s 29.1(1), l.347] "treaty lands" has the prescribed meaning
#ASSERT `s 29 how a term is defined` "treaty lands" `In all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters` EQUALS JUST `Has the prescribed meaning`
-- 464 [s 29.2(1), l.353] "Nisga'a Lisims Government" has the meaning in the Definitions Chapter of the Nisga'a Final Agreement
#ASSERT `s 29 how a term is defined` "Nisg̱a'a Lisims Government" `In an enactment` EQUALS JUST `Has the same meaning as in another enactment or agreement`
-- 465 [s 29.2(2), l.354] "Nisga'a Final Agreement" takes its meaning from the Nisga'a Final Agreement Act
#ASSERT `s 29 the words the Act gives for a term` "Nisg̱a'a Final Agreement" `In an enactment` EQUALS JUST "the same meaning as in the Nisg̱a'a Final Agreement Act"
-- 466 [s 29.2, l.353-354] "Nisga'a Region" (not listed) has a meaning given by this text: NC
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 29 the definition of a term names a thing` "Nisg̱a'a Region" `In an enactment` "anything"

§ `ss 30-33 (467-490)`

-- 467 [s 30, l.357] metric expression not mentioned in the Weights and Measures Act: the meaning in the International System of Units
#ASSERT `s 30 the meaning of a metric expression or symbol` NOTHING (JUST "SI meaning") EQUALS "SI meaning"
-- 467b [s 30, l.357] metric expression mentioned in the Weights and Measures Act: that meaning (it is read first)
#ASSERT `s 30 the meaning of a metric expression or symbol` (JUST "W and M meaning") (JUST "SI meaning") EQUALS "W and M meaning"
-- 468 [s 30, l.357] an imperial unit ("mile"): meaning given by this text: NC
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 30 the meaning of a metric expression or symbol` NOTHING NOTHING
-- 469 [s 31, l.360] a name commonly applied to a body means the body to which it is commonly applied
#ASSERT `s 31 what the commonly applied name means` "the House" "the Legislative Assembly" "the Legislative Assembly of British Columbia" EQUALS "the Legislative Assembly"
-- 470 [s 32(1) amended(a), l.365] repeal and replacement on the same subject matter counts as amended: Y
#ASSERT `s 32(1) a change to a domestic enactment counts as an amendment` (`A repeal` TRUE)
-- 471 [s 32(1) amended(b), l.366] revision or consolidation counts as amended: Y
#ASSERT `s 32(1) a change to a domestic enactment counts as an amendment` `A consolidation`
-- 472 [s 32(1) domestic enactment, l.367] an Act of another province of Canada is a domestic enactment: Y
#ASSERT `s 32(1) an enactment is a domestic enactment` `Another province of Canada`
-- 473 [s 32(1) domestic enactment, l.367] an Act of the United States is a domestic enactment: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 32(1) an enactment is a domestic enactment` `A jurisdiction outside Canada`)
-- 474 [s 32(1) foreign enactment, l.368] an Act of the United States is a foreign enactment: Y
#ASSERT `s 32(1) an enactment is a foreign enactment` `A jurisdiction outside Canada`
-- 475 [s 32(2), l.369] reference to an Ontario Act later amended: for a later transaction (2025-03-01) the amended text
#ASSERT `s 32 the day whose text of the named enactment the reference is to` (`A domestic enactment that has been amended, including by repeal and replacement on the same subject matter, revision or consolidation` (YMD 2025 3 1)) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 1
-- 477 [s 32(2),(3), l.369-370] ...the same where the Ontario Act was amended after the BC enactment came into force (transaction 2026-01-01)
#ASSERT `s 32 the day whose text of the named enactment the reference is to` (`A domestic enactment that has been amended, including by repeal and replacement on the same subject matter, revision or consolidation` (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
-- 478 [s 32(1),(2), l.365, 369] reference to a domestic Act repealed and replaced on the same subject matter: the replacement counts as an amendment
#ASSERT `s 32(1) a change to a domestic enactment counts as an amendment` (`A repeal` TRUE)
-- 479 [s 32(4), l.371] repealed and not replaced: for a later transaction, the Act as it read immediately before repeal (last day 2024-12-31)
#ASSERT `s 32 the day whose text of the named enactment the reference is to` (`A domestic enactment that has been repealed and not replaced with a domestic enactment on the same subject matter` (YMD 2024 12 31)) EQUALS YMD 2024 12 31
-- 480 [s 32(5), l.372] reference to a US statute: as it read on the day the BC enactment was enacted (2020-05-01)
#ASSERT `s 32 the day whose text of the named enactment the reference is to` (`A foreign enactment` (YMD 2020 5 1)) EQUALS YMD 2020 5 1
-- 481 [s 32(5), l.372] ...as it reads today (2026-10-13): N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 32 the day whose text of the named enactment the reference is to` (`A foreign enactment` (YMD 2020 5 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 13)
-- 484 [s 33(1), l.375] a series "sections 2 to 4" includes the first, 2: Y
#ASSERT `s 33(1) a number is in a series referred to by its first and last numbers` 2 4 2
-- 485 [s 33(1), l.375] ...includes the last, 4: Y
#ASSERT `s 33(1) a number is in a series referred to by its first and last numbers` 2 4 4
-- 486 [s 33(2), l.376] a reference to "section 5" is to section 5 of the enactment in which it occurs
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the enactment a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is a reference into` `A section` "the Foo Act" EQUALS "the Foo Act"
-- 487 [s 33(3), l.377] a reference to "paragraph (b)" is to a paragraph of the subsection in which it occurs
#ASSERT `s 33(3) the section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause is a reference into` `A paragraph` `In a subsection` EQUALS `In a subsection`
-- 488 [s 33(4), l.378] "the regulations" means regulations made under the enactment in which the reference occurs
#ASSERT `s 33(4) a reference to regulations is a reference to these regulations` "the Foo Act" "the Foo Act"
-- 489 [s 33(5), l.379] a reference by number to another enactment's section is read as printed under the King's Printer Act
#ASSERT `s 33(5) the division or line of the other enactment a reference by number or letter is a reference to` "s 5 as printed" "s 5 in another version" EQUALS "s 5 as printed"
-- 490 [s 33(6), l.380] "a licence under the Foo Act": "Act" includes regulations enacted under that Act: Y
#ASSERT `s 33(6) an Act in a reference to a matter under an Act includes the instrument` `A regulation enacted under the authority of that Act`

§ `ss 34-37 (491-513)`

-- 491 [s 34, l.383] an amending enactment is construed as part of the enactment it amends: Y
#ASSERT `s 34 the enactment is construed as part of the enactment that it amends` TRUE
-- 492 [s 35(1)(a), l.387] repeal revives an enactment not in force immediately before: N (the repeal leaves it unaffected)
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the repeal leaves the matter unaffected` `Reviving an enactment or thing not in force or existing immediately before the time when the repeal takes effect` FALSE
-- 493 [s 35(1)(b), l.388] repeal affects the previous operation of the repealed enactment: N
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the repeal leaves the matter unaffected` `The previous operation of the repealed enactment, or anything done or suffered under it` FALSE
-- 494 [s 35(1)(c), l.389] repeal affects a right acquired under it: N
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the repeal leaves the matter unaffected` `A right or obligation acquired, accrued, accruing or incurred under the repealed enactment` FALSE
-- 495 [s 35(1)(c), l.389] repeal affects an obligation accrued under it: N
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the repeal leaves the matter unaffected` `A right or obligation acquired, accrued, accruing or incurred under the repealed enactment` FALSE
-- 496 [s 35(1)(d), l.390] repeal affects an offence committed against the repealed enactment: N
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the repeal leaves the matter unaffected` `An offence committed against, or a contravention of, the repealed enactment, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred under it` FALSE
-- 497 [s 35(1)(d), l.390] repeal affects a penalty incurred under it: N
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the repeal leaves the matter unaffected` `An offence committed against, or a contravention of, the repealed enactment, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred under it` FALSE
-- 498 [s 35(1)(e), l.391] repeal affects an investigation, proceeding or remedy: N
#ASSERT `s 35(1) the repeal leaves the matter unaffected` `An investigation, proceeding or remedy for such a right, obligation, penalty, forfeiture or punishment` FALSE
-- 499 [s 35(2), l.392] proceeding may be instituted as if the enactment had not been repealed (no substitute): Y
#ASSERT `s 35(2) the basis on which an investigation, proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced` FALSE EQUALS `As if the enactment had not been repealed`
-- 500 [s 36(1)(a), l.396] repealed and substituted: a person acting under the former enactment continues to act until another is appointed: Y
#ASSERT `s 36(1)(a) a person acting under the former enactment must continue to act` TRUE FALSE
-- 501 [s 36(1)(b), l.397] a proceeding commenced under the former enactment is continued under the new, consistently: Y
#ASSERT `s 36(1)(b) the proceeding must be continued under and in conformity with the new enactment` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 502 [s 36(1)(c), l.398] the new procedure is followed in recovering penalties incurred under the former enactment: Y
#ASSERT `s 36(1)(c) the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed` `The recovery or enforcement of penalties and forfeitures incurred under the former enactment` TRUE TRUE
-- 503 [s 36(1)(d), l.399] new enactment reduces a penalty (1000 -> 500); imposed after the repeal: 500
#ASSERT `s 36(1)(d) the penalty that may be imposed or adjusted` 1000 500 TRUE EQUALS 500
-- 504 [s 36(1)(d), s 35(1)(d), l.399, 390] new enactment increases a penalty (500 -> 1000); imposed after the repeal: the former penalty 500 stands
#ASSERT `s 36(1)(d) the penalty that may be imposed or adjusted` 500 1000 TRUE EQUALS 500
-- 505 [s 36(1)(e), l.400] regulation under the former enactment remains in force insofar as not inconsistent: Y
#ASSERT `s 36(1)(e) a regulation made under the former enactment remains in force` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 506 [s 36(1)(e), l.400] a regulation inconsistent with the new enactment remains in force: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 36(1)(e) a regulation made under the former enactment remains in force` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- 509 [s 36(1), l.395] repeal WITHOUT substitution: s 36(1)(a) applies: N
-- RECONCILED 509: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT NOT (`s 36(1)(a) a person acting under the former enactment must continue to act` FALSE FALSE)`; triaged against the text: s 36(1) (l.395) applies only where another enactment is substituted for the repealed one (reviewer's verdict: its scenario wrong)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 36(1)(a) a person acting under the former enactment must continue to act` FALSE FALSE
-- 510 [s 37(1), l.405] a repeal is construed as a declaration that the enactment was previously in force: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Repeal of all or part of it` `A declaration that the enactment was, or was considered by those who enacted it to have been, previously in force`)
-- 511 [s 37(2), l.406] an amendment is construed as a declaration that the earlier law was different: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Amendment of it` `A declaration that the law under the enactment before the amendment was, or was considered by those who enacted it to have been, different from the law as amended`)
-- 512 [s 37(3), l.407] a re-enactment adopts the judicial construction of the language it re-uses: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Re-enactment of it` `An adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise`)
-- 513 [s 37(3), l.407] a consolidation adopts the judicial construction placed on similar language: N
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` `Consolidation of it` `An adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise`)

