#ASSERT `s 25.5(1) a day specified for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test: my holiday calendar` (YMD 2022 12 25) EQUALS YMD 2022 12 27
-- 566 [s 25.5(1), l.199] specified day Saturday 2022-12-24 -> 2022-12-24
#ASSERT `s 25.5(1) a day specified for doing an act, moved off a holiday` `test: my holiday calendar` (YMD 2022 12 24) EQUALS YMD 2022 12 24
-- 567 [s 25.1, l.169] born 2004-02-29 reaches age 4 on 2008-02-29
#ASSERT `s 25.1 the day a person reaches an age expressed in years` (YMD 2004 2 29) 4 EQUALS YMD 2008 2 29
-- 568 [s 26(1), l.203] Pacific Time 2025-03-01 17:00 as UTC -> 2025-03-02 00:00
#ASSERT `test: UTC moment is` (`s 26 the UTC moment of a Pacific Time moment` (`Pacific Time moment` WITH `calendar day` IS YMD 2025 3 1, `hour of the day` IS 17, `minute of the hour` IS 0)) (YMD 2025 3 2) 0
-- 569 [s 26(1), l.203] Pacific Time 2025-03-01 20:00 as UTC -> 2025-03-02 03:00
#ASSERT `test: UTC moment is` (`s 26 the UTC moment of a Pacific Time moment` (`Pacific Time moment` WITH `calendar day` IS YMD 2025 3 1, `hour of the day` IS 20, `minute of the hour` IS 0)) (YMD 2025 3 2) 3
-- 570 [s 25.2(3)(b), l.178] 2 clear weeks before 2025-03-15 -> 2025-02-28
#ASSERT `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of weeks` (YMD 2025 3 15) `The reference day is after the period` 2 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
-- 571 [s 25.3(2)(a), l.185] 6 clear months after 2025-08-15 -> 2026-02-16
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2025 8 15) `The reference day is before the period` 6 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 2 16
-- 572 [s 25.2(2), l.173] a period of 0 days after 2025-01-01: NC
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of days` (YMD 2025 1 1) `The reference day is before the period` 0 FALSE
-- 573 [s 25.4(1)(b), l.192] 1 year before 2025-01-01 -> 2024-01-01
#ASSERT `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2025 1 1) `The reference day is after the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2024 1 1
-- 574 [s 25.2(2)(a), l.174] 1 day after 2100-02-28 -> 2100-03-01
#ASSERT `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of days` (YMD 2100 2 28) `The reference day is before the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2100 3 1
-- 575 [s 25.2(2)(a), l.174] 1 day after 2000-02-28 -> 2000-02-29
#ASSERT `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of days` (YMD 2000 2 28) `The reference day is before the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2000 2 29
-- 576 [s 25.3(3), l.187] 1 month after 2100-01-31 -> 2100-02-28
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2100 1 31) `The reference day is before the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2100 2 28

§ `GAP register (no assertion written; the encoding exports no function that can be asked the scenario)`

-- GAP 45 [s 4(3)]  the enactment is in effect during the whole of its last day: no predicate "in effect at a moment".
-- GAP 47 [s 4(2)]  the replaced enactment is in effect throughout the day before the new one commences: same.
-- GAP 49 [s 4(4), s 35] rights accrued under an expired enactment survive: s 4(4) and s 35 are separate functions with no composition.
-- GAP 50 [s 5(1)]  the power may be exercised before commencement: only the effect of the thing done is encoded.
-- GAP 53 [s 5(1)]  a power not conferred to make the enactment effective: no input says why the power was conferred.
-- GAP 62, 63 [s 8] every enactment is remedial; a penal enactment is not excluded: only `s 8 the construction to give to an enactment` (choose among candidates) exists.
-- GAP 72 [s 9]  preamble overriding a clear operative provision (NC): no function.
-- GAP 73 [s 10] the enacting clause is not mandatory: only "may be in this form" is asked, which cannot say that another form is allowed.
-- GAP 80, 81, 82 [s 11(3)] LGIC regulation amending a minister's name, a ministry's name, a penalty: no function for s 11(3).
-- GAP 87 [s 13 with s 2(1)] a regulation defining the term itself: `s 13` takes only the authorizing enactment's meaning.
-- GAP 147 [s 20(4)(b),(c)] term ends 2025-12-31 but an enactment terminates it 2025-09-15: no function combines the limbs.
-- GAP 148 [s 20(4)] appointee terminates earlier: the module says the caller supplies the day.
-- GAP 260, 261 [s 29 year] a 12-month period from 2025-06-01 is a "year", and is not a "calendar year": no predicate (only the last day of a year, and the calendar-year days).
-- GAP 292, 293, 294 [s 29 holiday(d), (a), (b)] a day set by Parliament or appointed by proclamation as a holiday; the date of Good Friday, Easter Monday, Victoria Day, British Columbia Day, Labour Day or Family Day in a year (NC): the calendar is an input; no date-to-named-holiday function. Scenarios 286-290 (Christmas Day, New Year's Day, Canada Day, 30 September, Remembrance Day) are asserted only as list membership, not as dates.
-- GAP 300 [s 26(2)] a reference to time in BC is a reference to Pacific Time: no function.
-- GAP 301, 302, 303 [s 26(1)] UTC moment to Pacific Time: only Pacific to UTC exists.
-- GAP 339 [s 29 affidavit] "swear" includes solemnly declare or affirm: not in the catalogue as a thing.
-- GAP 391 [s 29 minister] a member of the Legislative Assembly who is not in the Executive Council is not a minister: no function.
-- GAP 393 [s 29 minor] the age of majority as a number (NC): the caller supplies it.
-- GAP 425 [s 29 record] an electronic file is a record: the catalogue is a list of strings; an instance of a general limb cannot be classified.
-- GAP 439 [s 29 savings institution(e)] limb (e) repealed: not modelled.
-- GAP 457 [s 29.1 settlement legislation] a regulation is not settlement legislation: no function.
-- GAP 460 [s 29.1(2)] repealed: not modelled.
-- GAP 461, 462, 463 [s 29.1(3),(4)] LGIC regulations defining treaty lands: no function.
-- GAP 476 [s 32(3)] the same where amended before the BC enactment came into force: no input records the timing, so 475 and 477 are asserted only.
-- GAP 482, 483 [s 32(2)] reference for a transaction before the amendment (NC); reference in a repealed BC enactment: no function.
-- GAP 507, 508 [s 36(1)(f), (2)] repealed: not modelled.
-- GAP 525 [s 41(1)(d)] a fee the enactment does not authorize: the list item has no input for authorization.
-- GAP 544 [Schedule] the Schedule gives map coordinates: no function.
-- GAP 545, 546, 548, 549 [ss 25-25.5, s 29 year] 5 business days; 48 hours; fiscal year; fortnight (NC): no function can be asked, so no refusal can be asserted.
